<title>USA: Benjamin Taylor to take helm at Boston Globe.</title>
<headline>Benjamin Taylor to take helm at Boston Globe.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Times Co subsidiary The Boston Globe said on Thursday that its president, Benjamin Taylor, will also become its publisher, effective April 1.</p>
<p>Taylor, 49, will succeed his cousin, William O. Taylor, 64, who was recently elected to the board of the directors of the Boston Federal Reserve Bank.</p>
<p>Taylor, who will also keep his title as president, will become the fifth family member to hold the position of publisher since the newspaper was founded in 1872.</p>
<p>--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106</p>
